# Agential Skill — Windsurf Rules

Use this self-contained editorial standard for every frontend task. The target is minimal image-led design, not a SaaS template.

- Read `context.md` first; update it after design decisions and milestones.
- Read the relevant internal baseline guidance before coding.
- Use full-bleed photography or texture, oversized neutral grotesque type, hard-edged rectangular framing, visible 1px construction grids, sparse navigation, and concise copy.
- Use architectural rectangular geometry throughout. Avoid soft corners, pills, capsules, circles, and ornamental shapes.
- No floating cards, bento layouts, shadows, blur/glass, gradients, equal rows, icon boxes, or generic dashboard widgets. Use flat planes, split stages, image strips, wireframe matrices, and ledger rows.
- Palette: black, white, charcoal, cream, and selective vermilion/red/orange. Body copy is neutral; no blue/cyan/purple copy.
- One focal idea per section. Headings 1–6 words; utility labels 9–11px; metadata sparse; media uses `object-cover` with `3/4`, `4/5`, or `16/9` ratios.
- Interactions use real state, linear motion, keyboard semantics, square focus indicators, and reduced-motion support.
- Review every diff and run available validation before reporting completion.
